vayu: Novatek NT36672C touchscreen over bit-banged SPI (patch 0157)

New bsd/dev/vayu_touch.c. The touch IC sits on SE17 (spi@c80000, GPIO55-58),
reset GPIO12, IRQ GPIO122. SE17 is provisioned for GSI DMA, so the pins are
driven as GPIOs and the GENI block is left alone. The IC has no flash: the
driver writes j20s_novatek_ts_fw02.bin (from /chosen "gpufw,<name>", i.e. the
mkpayload.py --gpufw directory) into its SRAM with the hw-CRC boot flow of
Xiaomi's nt36672c driver, then polls the 65-byte event buffer on a latched
TLMM rising-edge status and feeds SweetHID. Boot-args: vayutouch=0,
vayutouchdelay=N, vayutouchlog=1, vayutouchfw=NAME.

